                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Point `reenter` at a keeper app and one of its upkeeps.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "reenter",
            "args": [],
            "returns": {
                "type": "uint64"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Call the keeper's `execute` back, from inside its own execution.\nArchon writes an upkeep's state before submitting the inner call, so a re-entrant execution has to satisfy the schedule afresh. Whether that is enough to stop one \u2014 and who a nested execution pays, given the sender it sees is this app rather than the keeper \u2014 is measured in `scripts/spike_reentrancy.py` rather than argued about.\nRe-enters once and only once: unconditional recursion would just hit the AVM's depth limit and tell us nothing.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
